WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:01.480
Hey, David.

00:00:01.480 --> 00:00:02.480
On balance.

00:00:02.480 --> 00:00:06.930
Do you think that the protests help or hurt
Donald Trump?

00:00:06.930 --> 00:00:08.130
I think that they hurt him.

00:00:08.130 --> 00:00:12.059
I believe that early the idea that Trump had
was that they would help.

00:00:12.059 --> 00:00:14.070
I just think he miscalculated.

00:00:14.070 --> 00:00:20.670
There is no question that when you see protests,
some small portion of which end up having

00:00:20.670 --> 00:00:21.670
some.

00:00:21.670 --> 00:00:26.940
Violent elements and arrests taking place,
arson, looting, etc..

00:00:26.940 --> 00:00:29.000
Certainly Trump's base is activated.

00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:31.380
They are motivated.

00:00:31.380 --> 00:00:34.460
They become more enthusiastic about voting
for Donald Trump.

00:00:34.460 --> 00:00:36.050
I don't deny that.

00:00:36.050 --> 00:00:39.690
The problem is I think that the protests are
really hurting Trump with everybody who is

00:00:39.690 --> 00:00:41.140
not already committed to him.

00:00:41.140 --> 00:00:46.739
And if you only are pleasing the people already
voting for you, you can't make up a three,

00:00:46.739 --> 00:00:51.880
five, seven or nine point popular vote deficit,
which is what different polls claim.

00:00:51.880 --> 00:00:54.559
Donald Trump is currently experiencing.

00:00:54.559 --> 00:00:56.890
Most people aren't falling for.

00:00:56.890 --> 00:01:02.160
If you see a violent confrontation in Portland,
that's what you will have under Joe Biden's

00:01:02.160 --> 00:01:03.280
America.

00:01:03.280 --> 00:01:04.700
Most people aren't falling for that.

00:01:04.700 --> 00:01:06.210
Most people are accurately recognizing.

00:01:06.210 --> 00:01:07.210
Wait a second.

00:01:07.210 --> 00:01:10.530
Biden's America trumps president right now.

00:01:10.530 --> 00:01:13.510
This is happening in Trump's America right
now.

00:01:13.510 --> 00:01:18.730
And it reminds me a little bit of the situation
when Donald Trump was asked about early in

00:01:18.730 --> 00:01:20.700
Corona virus, earlier in Corona virus.

00:01:20.700 --> 00:01:23.310
Do you take responsibility for this or that?

00:01:23.310 --> 00:01:25.990
And Trump said, I take no responsibility at
all.

00:01:25.990 --> 00:01:33.920
Apply that logic to the protests and to the
elements of the protests that have been violent,

00:01:33.920 --> 00:01:36.140
which, again, is very, very small.

00:01:36.140 --> 00:01:41.010
And Trump actually spotlights those incidents,
thinking it will hurt Joe Biden.

00:01:41.010 --> 00:01:43.560
And he says it's Biden's fault that this is
happening.

00:01:43.560 --> 00:01:46.180
It's radical Marxists fault that this is happening.

00:01:46.180 --> 00:01:48.610
And it will be even worse if they win.

00:01:48.610 --> 00:01:51.780
It's backfiring because it doesn't pass the
sniff test.

00:01:51.780 --> 00:01:56.520
And what this ultimately gets back to is that
Donald Trump was a much stronger candidate,

00:01:56.520 --> 00:02:01.980
running as an insurgent who had not had a
career in politics and who could sort of credibly

00:02:01.980 --> 00:02:05.140
criticize whoever is running and whoever is
in power.

00:02:05.140 --> 00:02:09.450
Trump's been president now for four years,
and yet he's still trying to run like an insurgent.

00:02:09.450 --> 00:02:15.239
Trump is still saying, you've got to reelect
me so I can do the wall and do health care

00:02:15.239 --> 00:02:18.060
and do more taxes and all of this other stuff.

00:02:18.060 --> 00:02:23.410
He's been president for four years, and it's
a gambit that I believe has failed him.

00:02:23.410 --> 00:02:28.750
He may still win for other reasons, but I
think continuing to run as an outsider, even

00:02:28.750 --> 00:02:32.120
though he's been president now for four years,
I think it's a mistake.

00:02:32.120 --> 00:02:39.250
And if you look at the polling data, you see
it when the unrest happened in Wisconsin.

00:02:39.250 --> 00:02:44.680
There were people saying this is going to
hurt Joe Biden and it's going to hurt Democrats.

00:02:44.680 --> 00:02:49.370
You had enlightened, centrist grifter's, right.

00:02:49.370 --> 00:02:51.860
Saying Trump just won.

00:02:51.860 --> 00:02:56.079
The Senate is going to stay Republican because
of what's going on in Wisconsin.

00:02:56.079 --> 00:03:00.879
A lot of pundits jumped all over that, not
pun dense, as some say, pundits.

00:03:00.879 --> 00:03:03.489
Come on, we know the word p0 NDIC.

00:03:03.489 --> 00:03:09.389
And in fact, Joe Biden is polling slightly
better today in Wisconsin than he was when

00:03:09.389 --> 00:03:10.849
Jacob Blache got shot.

00:03:10.849 --> 00:03:11.849
It's marginal.

00:03:11.849 --> 00:03:14.040
It's a small it's a small delta.

00:03:14.040 --> 00:03:17.920
But things have not gotten worse for Joe Biden
in Wisconsin since that happened.

00:03:17.920 --> 00:03:20.970
And I think that what's happening are two
different things.

00:03:20.970 --> 00:03:26.670
One, most people aren't buying that what we're
seeing has anything to do with Joe Biden.

00:03:26.670 --> 00:03:30.650
It's happening under Donald Trump and Trump's
actions have actually worsened it.

00:03:30.650 --> 00:03:38.499
When Trump sent federal agents like jack booted
thugs to areas with unrest to carry out, you

00:03:38.499 --> 00:03:44.110
know, authoritarian Soviet style tactics,
throwing people into vans and all of this

00:03:44.110 --> 00:03:51.500
stuff, he could have instead used the bully
pulpit to say we are demanding federal investigations

00:03:51.500 --> 00:03:54.000
of the police officers and departments involved.

00:03:54.000 --> 00:03:58.859
This is not what the next four years are going
to look like in America.

00:03:58.859 --> 00:04:01.180
He could have listened to people on systemic
race it.

00:04:01.180 --> 00:04:02.180
Right.

00:04:02.180 --> 00:04:03.180
He could have done it differently.

00:04:03.180 --> 00:04:06.409
And I think he'd be cruising to reelection
if he had done that and paid more attention

00:04:06.409 --> 00:04:08.459
to the virus for sure.

00:04:08.459 --> 00:04:10.939
But instead, he didn't do that.

00:04:10.939 --> 00:04:18.600
And it it has made it it has fomented the
feeling that things are unstable and instability

00:04:18.600 --> 00:04:20.850
tends not to be good for the incumbent.

00:04:20.850 --> 00:04:22.110
So that's my bottom line.

00:04:22.110 --> 00:04:28.410
I think that Donald Trump's base is certainly
enthusiastically going to vote for Trump because

00:04:28.410 --> 00:04:31.160
of the protests, but they were going to vote
for Trump anyway.

00:04:31.160 --> 00:04:33.940
Maybe they're just doing it slightly more
enthusiastically.

00:04:33.940 --> 00:04:37.950
I think with everybody else, the protests
have been very, very bad for Donald Trump.

